commit 21c4876a98a8c70e33d6a1bbd54f56c7e00fd6a9

C03: a results-page navigation names the search it opened, and a quoted result title is not a restated definition ask (WEB1483)

WEB1481 measured two defects. The verified navigations to YouTube's results page ended with «Abrí YouTube en el navegador» — the very example the navigation instruction offered — hiding the search the person asked for; `_opened_search_in_navigation` now reads the site and query of a verified results-page address (YouTube results, Bing search) and the instruction demands reporting that search with its exact query, never the bare site. «Investiga en internet que es el h2o» composed «H2O es una molécula… como indica la página Wikipedia…» six times and the App rejected each as internal_code: the quoted result title «¿Qué significa H2O?» contains «que significa» and LooksLikeRestatingDefinitionAsk read the raw text; it and LooksLikeMachineSlotAsk now read the vocabulary text where observed result titles are masked (ObservedResponseLiterals).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


